From c7b61b5f62e05e18864e6693b0bb2ad9ef9012a4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: primez <mpincoski@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 06:24:22 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] [HLSTree] Sum the exact EXTINF durations for the segment
 times

The parser truncated each EXTINF duration to whole ms at float precision
and chained the next segment from the truncated end. With EXTINF values
such as 4.5045 or 6.006, the segment times drifted from the media time,
about 0.18 s after 44 minutes of a real stream. A seek 40 ms before a
segment start then converted the seek time with the diff of the current
segment and continued at the next segment.

Each segment time is now the exact sum of the durations since the last
EXT-X-PROGRAM-DATE-TIME, rounded to ms. FixMediaSequence and
FixDiscSequence compute the same sums, so they still match the segment
times.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
